Subject: drm/amdgpu: fail MODE1/MODE2 resets that have no implementation

On ASICs whose PSP has no mode1_reset callback, a MODE1 reset through PSP
reports success without touching the hardware: psp_mode1_reset() is

	((psp)->funcs->mode1_reset ? (psp)->funcs->mode1_reset((psp)) : false)

and false is 0. Likewise smu_mode2_reset() returns 0 when the ppt table has no
mode2_reset. On Cyan Skillfish2 both apply (psp_v11_0_8_funcs has only ring
callbacks, cyan_skillfish_ppt_funcs has no mode2_reset), and nv_asic_reset()
selects MODE1 by default, so "GPU reset succeeded, trying to resume" is logged
within about 0.1 ms and the driver re-initialises IP blocks on a GPU that was
never reset.

On an AMD BC-250 this hangs the host during resume in every deliberate reset
on record (20 trials across the debugfs and KFD entry points), usually on the
first GC register access. Register state confirms no reset took place: a GC register that
the driver writes from 0x7 to 0x1f at probe still reads 0x1f when resume runs.

Return -EOPNOTSUPP when the callback that would perform the reset does not
exist, so recovery fails visibly instead of resuming live hardware. Tested
on the same board (as a runtime-switchable equivalent): four deliberate
resets, two MODE1 and two MODE2, each failed with -95, the host stayed up,
and a compute job ran afterwards. A subsequent reboot stalled in shutdown
every time, which this patch does not address.

---
Against torvalds/linux 587858367581 (2026-09-14). Callers audited:
every in-tree ppt table reached through a default MODE2 path provides
mode2_reset; of the PSP versions, v11_0_8, v13_0, v13_0_4, v14_0, v15_0 and
v15_0_8 have no mode1_reset, and the ones used by dGPUs reach MODE1 through
the SMU instead. Board test: logs/reset-honest-2026-09-15/ (section B).

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_device.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_device.c
@@ -4961,7 +4961,13 @@
 		ret = amdgpu_dpm_mode1_reset(adev);
 	} else {
 		dev_info(adev->dev, "GPU psp mode1 reset\n");
-		ret = psp_gpu_reset(adev);
+		if (adev->firmware.load_type == AMDGPU_FW_LOAD_PSP &&
+		    !adev->psp.funcs->mode1_reset) {
+			dev_err(adev->dev, "PSP mode1 reset is not implemented for this ASIC\n");
+			ret = -EOPNOTSUPP;
+		} else {
+			ret = psp_gpu_reset(adev);
+		}
 	}
 
 	if (ret)
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/pm/swsmu/amdgpu_smu.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/pm/swsmu/amdgpu_smu.c
@@ -3616,8 +3616,10 @@
 	if (!smu->pm_enabled)
 		return -EOPNOTSUPP;
 
-	if (smu->ppt_funcs->mode2_reset)
-		ret = smu->ppt_funcs->mode2_reset(smu);
+	if (!smu->ppt_funcs->mode2_reset)
+		return -EOPNOTSUPP;
+
+	ret = smu->ppt_funcs->mode2_reset(smu);
 
 	if (ret)
 		dev_err(smu->adev->dev, "Mode2 reset failed!\n");
